    <string name="app_name">PumaRun</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_title">PumaRun privacy policy</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_button">Privacy policy</string>
    <string name="close">Close</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_body">Last updated: October 1, 2026.\n\nPumaRun uses device location while you use the running features. Location is used to show your position, measure distance and pace, draw your route, and save a completed run on your device.\n\nPumaRun does not create accounts, run advertising, sell personal data, or upload your routes to a PumaRun server. Saved runs remain on this device until you delete them from Tracks or uninstall the app.\n\nThe map loads OpenStreetMap map tiles. Requests for those tiles can reveal the approximate map area being viewed to the map tile provider. OpenStreetMap data is provided under the Open Database License; attribution is shown on every map.\n\nText-to-speech announcements are handled by the text-to-speech engine selected on your device. Depending on that engine, speech processing may be local or provided by its vendor.\n\nPumaRun requests location and notification permissions only for the run experience. You can revoke permissions in Android settings. For privacy questions, contact the developer through the PumaRun Play Store listing or https://github.com/wecalderonc/PumaRun.</string>

